WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.690
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday; it's Question
Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.340
from real nerdfighters, let's get right to
it.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.811
What's the cheesiest joke you know?

00:00:06.811 --> 00:00:08.760
You know what kind of cheese can perform miracles?

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.110
Cheesus of Nazareth.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.110
Who the eff is-

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.110
Wait, wait!

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.110
I got a better one.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.600
What happened after the French cheese factory
exploded?

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.160
There was debris everywhere.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.920
You got any new books coming?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:18.920
I'm trying.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.870
Hey, in TFiOS, did you name Isaac that because
his eyes are sick?

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.870
No.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.080
Unfortunately, I'm not that punny, except
when it comes to cheese jokes.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.680
I named Isaac after the guy in the Hebrew
Bible who also went blind.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.930
How excited are you that the TFiOS DVD comes
out tomorrow?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.930
Good news, friend.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:37.030
Tomorrow is now today, and I am very excited
because, at last, people can see my brilliant

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.550
acting in the extended cut.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.610
Will you ever appear in a movie of your books?

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.610
I have!

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.399
I had a cameo in The Fault in Our Stars movie,
but it got cut, because my screen presence

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:45.399
was too powerful.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:48.280
They felt like people wouldn't be able to
pay attention to Hazel's love affair with

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.550
Augustus because they would be distracted
by the camera's love affair with me.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.649
Any news about the Looking For Alaska or Paper
Towns movies?

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:57.500
So I don't know much about Looking For Alaska,
but Paper Towns looks like it is really really

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.090
going to happen, like, they hired a director,
the brilliant Jake Schreier who made Robot

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.090
and Frank.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.039
The screenplay by the guys who wrote TFiOS
is amazing, my friend Nat Wolff is going to

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:09.299
play Q, and supposedly it's going to come
out on July 31, so I... it might actually

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:10.299
happen!

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:11.969
If you could change anything about your books,
what would it be?

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:15.670
Uh, the word "deadpan" appears like twelve
times in Looking for Alaska, which in retrospect

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.689
is probably eleven times too many.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:19.380
How do I pass AP Chemistry?

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.520
Crash Course might help!

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.520
Who's your favorite Beatle?

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.960
What color would you be if you could be any
color?

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.429
I promise these were right next to each other
in my timeline!

00:01:25.429 --> 00:01:26.429
John, Green!

00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:28.979
Are oranges named after orange, or is orange
named after oranges?

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:32.259
The name of the fruit preceded the name of
the color by at least two hundred years.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.259
Bananas or pineapple?

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.349
I guess we've reached the fruit portion of
Question Tuesday.

00:01:35.349 --> 00:01:36.349
Bananas!

00:01:36.349 --> 00:01:37.740
Will there be a nerdfighter meet-up soon?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.439
There are location-specific nerdfighter group
all around the world, link in the doobly-doo,

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:45.270
there are lots and lots of gatherings, I've
always had a good time at them, check it out!

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.499
Why you love the metaphors?

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:50.399
I would argue that most humans love metaphors,
because so much human thinking is symbolic.

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:54.549
Like, we imagine a meningitis headache as
a "vice gripping our head".

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:58.309
And if we can imagine, like, particularly
original or compelling metaphors, it can help

00:01:58.309 --> 00:02:00.399
people to imagine what we're feeling!

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:04.369
So good metaphors make my experiences more
real to you, and yours more real to me, which

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:06.309
is kind of what language is supposed to do,
right?

00:02:06.309 --> 00:02:08.810
Can you make a metaphor using the word "slay"?

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.180
Now, this is not my area of expertise, but
I'm pretty sure the colloquial use of the

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.540
word "slay" is already metaphoric.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.200
I mean, I don't think that new Taylor Swift
song actually killed you.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.460
But we say that it "slayed" us, because the
experience of it was so awesome that now we

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.060
are... metaphorically dead.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:26.400
I'm not saying it's a great metaphor, but
it is a metaphor!

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.930
Pizza or Ansel Elgort?

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.130
Ansel Elgort on pizza.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.879
Ansel Elgort on pizza is not an acceptable
answer.

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:33.560
Hmm, then I'm going to go with Ansel Elgort
slathered in pizza.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:34.560
Hey, review Hank's album.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.079
It's Hank Green's best album to date, The
Perfect Strangers bring a punk rock energy

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:40.359
to Hank's quick-witted and lyric-driven songwriting.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:41.980
I give it five out of five stars.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.830
It's actually Henry's second-favorite album,
behind only the Phineas and Ferb Star Wars

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:46.830
album.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.870
Aren't you and Hank supposed to do a punishment?

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:48.870
Well, I owe one.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.870
Hank, what's my punishment?

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.239
How'd you decide on baby names?

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:52.659
We just stole our grandparents' names.

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:54.020
How many boys are in One Direction?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.630
What is this, a quiz show?

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.840
There's Harry, and Niall, and Liam... ah...

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:00.840
Zayn!

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.840
Four?

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.810
Wait, NONE!

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:04.810
None!

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.140
There are no boys in One Direction, they are
all adults!

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.379
Hey, how many books can you balance on your
head?

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:11.170
S... seven, but not for very long!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.420
Tell your son he's really cute.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.420
Hey, Henry!

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.319
A stranger on the Internet says that you're
cute.

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:19.709
How do I get my three-year-old to eat anything
other than PBJ, pizza, and macaroni?

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:21.920
You can get your three-year-old to eat three
different foods?

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.920
Are you a wizard?!

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.830
What colour - unnecessary "u" - are your socks?

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:25.830
Many-colored happy socks!

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.599
Are signed posters really signed, or just
digitally?

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:32.299
When I say that something is signed, I mean
that I signed it, like with my hand, and a

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:33.299
pen.

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:34.299
Writing font?

00:03:34.299 --> 00:03:35.299
Arial.

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:36.299
Thoughts on WheezyWaiter's latest video?

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:37.299
Awwwwww.

00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:38.299
Favorite HP book and movie?

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:39.299
Four comma eight.

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:40.299
What's your favorite dinosaur?

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:43.030
Stegosaurus, because when I was a kid, paleontologists
thought that it had two brains, a head brain

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.030
and a butt brain.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.129
And there was nothing in the world funnier
to me than the idea of a butt brain.

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:48.129
I have a question.

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:50.319
Mmm... that's not a question, Maureen, that's
a statement.

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:51.319
And so is this:

00:03:51.319 --> 00:03:52.090
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

